UPDATE companies SET description='Industrial Steel & Wire Co. LLC (ISW) is a third-generation, family-owned wire distributor headquartered in Bristol, Connecticut. The company was founded in 1935 by Dr. Harry Furlong in Chicago, Illinois, as Industrial Steel Wire Company. It remains under the leadership of the Furlong family, with Dr. Brian K. Furlong serving as president.

ISW stocks and distributes a broad range of wire products—including stainless steel, carbon steel, music wire, basic wire, non-ferrous wire, cold-heading quality, and specialty grades—across six North American service centers totaling 400,000 square feet of warehouse space. The company provides value-added processing such as torsion straightening (diameters .0300–.1250 in), cut-to-length, slitting, tension leveling, and multiple packaging options (continuous coils, catch-weight coils, reel-less cores, reels, and spools).

The company emphasizes its “ISW Pledge” of service, trust, selection, and response—principles dating to Harry Furlong’s original goal of earning customer confidence with every order. Differentiators include one-hour quotes, same-day shipping on stocked items, and a network of six strategically located warehouses to ensure rapid delivery.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire distribution", "Torsion straightening", "Cut-to-length", "Slitting", "Tension leveling", "Packaging services", "Cold heading quality wire supply", "Straighten and cut wire", "Strip products supply"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Stainless Steel", "Carbon Steel", "Music Wire", "Basic Wire", "Non-Ferrous Wire", "Cold Heading Quality Wire", "Specialty Grade Wire", "Strip Products"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping on stocked items; one-hour quotes", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Third-generation family-owned wire distributor", "Six strategically located service centers across North America", "400,000 sq ft of inventory ready to ship", "One-hour quotes and same-day shipping on stocked items", "Torsion straightening and cut-to-length services"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1935 by Dr. Harry Furlong in Chicago -> /about", "Third-generation family-owned business -> /", "Six North American warehouse locations (Bristol CT, Chicago IL, Cleveland OH, Lewisburg TN, Toronto ONT, Queretaro MEX) -> /", "400,000 sq ft warehouse space -> /", "Torsion straightening capabilities: diameter .0300\u2013.1250 in, all grades except Oil Tempered, Chrome Silicon, Basic 1008, Basic Galvanized -> /", "Packaging services: continuous coils on carriers, catch weight/mill coils, reel-less cores, reels, spools -> /", "Headquarters in Bristol, CT -> db", "Wire distributor with value-added services (cut-to-length, slitting, tension leveling) -> /about", "Dr. Brian K. Furlong is President -> /about", "Materials: stainless steel, carbon steel, music wire, basic wire, non-ferrous wire, cold heading quality, specialty grade -> /", "Same-day shipping and one-hour quotes -> /", "Family-owned and operated -> /about", "Timeline includes 1935 founding, 1976 Bristol branch, 1987 Star Steel & Wire purchase, 2012 cold heading wire addition -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We''re a third generation, family owned business. We focus on being the agile, flexible wire distribution partner that you can count on.", "founded_year": "1935", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='industrial-steel-wire-co-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Indy Solar Solutions operates from Indianapolis, Indiana, as a locally owned small business serving homeowners and businesses across the state. The company was founded to help Hoosiers take control of energy costs through clean, reliable solar power, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The firm designs and installs custom solar photovoltaic systems paired with battery backup, handling every step from initial site assessment and 3D modeling through permitting, utility interconnection, and final activation. In addition to new installations, it offers a dedicated solar panel cleaning service using specialized equipment to maintain peak production. The team works with high-quality solar panels and battery storage hardware, and assists customers with financing options including $0-down programs and federal tax credit navigation.

Its primary customers are residential property owners in Indiana, though the company also references commercial projects of varying scale. Typical engagements range from single-family rooftop arrays to larger business installations, all tailored to the specific energy usage, roof geometry, and shading conditions of each site.

Indy Solar Solutions distinguishes itself by emphasizing local presence and direct communication, positioning itself as an alternative to national chains. It promotes transparent pricing, a single point of contact from design to energization, and a commitment to honest workmanship backed by a small-business ethos.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design", "Permitting and utility interconnection", "Residential solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Battery backup integration", "Solar panel cleaning", "Financing and tax credit assistance"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Solar panels", "Battery storage systems"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "1 day to several weeks for installation", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Locally owned small business", "Handles design through utility approval", "Offers $0 down financing", "Provides solar panel cleaning service", "Uses high-quality equipment"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Indianapolis, Indiana -> /", "Ownership: locally owned small business -> /", "Services: solar installation, solar panel cleaning, design, permitting, utility approval -> /", "Industries served: residential and commercial -> /", "Lead time: installation takes one day to several weeks -> /", "Differentiators: not a national chain, honest work, clear communication, high-quality equipment, $0 down financing -> /", "Materials: solar panels, battery storage -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We offer both solar installations and solar panel cleaning services. Our team designs and installs custom solar systems for homes and businesses using high-quality materials and equipment.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='indy-solar-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Indy Urban Hardwood Company operates from Indianapolis, Indiana, where it was founded in 2017 by Brian Presnell. The venture began as a response to the emerald ash borer infestation that was killing the city''s ash trees, with the goal of giving those trees a second life as studio furniture.

The company fabricates handcrafted solid wood furniture using 100 percent recycled lumber sourced exclusively from the Indianapolis metropolitan area.

The furniture serves a range of public and private spaces, with concrete examples including office buildings, libraries, restaurants, and music venues throughout Indianapolis. Residential clients are also served, reflecting the company''s broader market reach.

