UPDATE companies SET description='Infraredx, based in Bedford, Massachusetts, has been developing intravascular imaging technologies for nearly 30 years. The company was acquired by Nipro Corporation in 2015 and operates as a subsidiary within Nipro''s Vascular Division.

The company designs and manufactures catheter-based imaging systems that combine intravascular ultrasound (IVUS) with near-infrared spectroscopy (NIRS). Its flagship Makoto platform integrates high-resolution structural imaging with plaque compositional analysis, while the Clarispro HD-IVUS and Dualpro IVUS+NIRS systems address specific clinical needs. Essential accessories support the imaging catheters. No facility size, headcount, or production volumes are disclosed.

The technology is used in clinical studies such as SPECTAL and COLOR, which supported 510(k) clearances. Customers include opinion leaders in cardiology who collaborate on defining new standards of care.

