UPDATE companies SET description='Integra Technologies operates from Wichita, Kansas, where it has provided semiconductor assembly and test services for over 40 years. The company was acquired by Micross in January 2025 and continues as an independent subsidiary.

The company delivers full turnkey semiconductor test and assembly services, covering die preparation (wafer thinning, dicing, pick-and-place, inspection), packaging and assembly (system-in-package, multi-chip modules, die attach, flip-chip interconnect, encapsulation), electrical test (wafer probe, singulated die probe, up-screening, custom ASIC/FPGA test), reliability qualification (PEM qualification, copper wire evaluation, ESD, CGA interconnect, burn-in, temperature cycling, thermal shock), destructive physical analysis, failure analysis, laser ablation, counterfeit detection, obsolescence management, and a parts management program. Mirrored assembly and test lines provide redundancy. Integra describes itself as the largest U.S. OSAT provider.

Integra serves the aerospace, defense, space, medical, automotive, and communications sectors, focusing on high-reliability applications where failure is not an option. As a DMEA DoD Source OSAT provider, it supports U.S.-based electronics manufacturers requiring secure, domestic supply chains.

The company emphasizes its end-to-end, 100% U.S.-based model as a differentiator, enabling tariff-free procurement, accelerated time to market, and lower costs through vendor consolidation. It states that no other competitor offers the same breadth of end-to-end solutions for the high-reliability market.', certifications=ARRAY['DMEA DoD Trusted Source OSAT provider']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wafer thinning", "Wafer dicing", "Pick & place", "Die inspection", "System-in-package (SiP) assembly", "Multi-chip module (MCM) assembly", "Die attach", "Standard IC packaging", "Flip-chip interconnect", "Encapsulation", "Wafer probe", "Singulated die probe", "Device up-screening", "Custom ASIC/FPGA test", "PEM qualification", "Copper wire evaluation", "ESD testing", "CGA interconnect", "Burn-in", "Temperature cycling", "Thermal shock", "Destructive physical analysis (DPA)", "Failure analysis", "Laser ablation", "Counterfeit detection", "Obsolescence management", "BOM management", "Parts Management Program (PMP)", "SEM analysis", "Mechanical testing", "Metallurgical analysis"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Space", "Medical", "Automotive", "Communications", "High-reliability microelectronics"], "materials": ["Semiconductor wafers", "Die", "IC packages", "Flip-chip interconnect materials", "Encapsulation materials"], "equipment": ["SEM Lab", "Mechanical Lab", "Metallurgical Lab", "Specialty Lab"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest U.S. OSAT provider", "100% U.S.-based end-to-end services under one roof", "DMEA DoD Trusted Source OSAT provider", "Mirrored assembly and test capabilities for redundancy", "Tariff-free procurement for domestic manufacturers"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Wichita, Kansas -> db", "Over 40 years of operation -> /about-us", "Acquired by Micross January 2025 -> /about-us", "Independent subsidiary of Micross -> /", "Largest U.S. OSAT provider -> /about-us", "Full turnkey semiconductor test & assem