sks, nightstands; Storage Solutions: Dressers, chests of drawers, wardrobes, custom closets; Beds: Headboards, platform beds, custom bed frames; Cabinetry: Kitchen cabinets, bathroom vanities, built-in bookshelves, entertainment centers; Libraries: Custom built in shelving / storage / lighting", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-leftwich-custom-furniture-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Jif® peanut butter brand, owned by J.M. Smucker Co., has been headquartered in Lexington, Kentucky since its national launch in 1958. The brand debuted with creamy-smooth and crunchy varieties, establishing a presence that has grown over more than six decades.

The company produces a range of peanut butter products including creamy, extra crunchy, natural, reduced-fat, low-sodium (Simply Jif®), and chocolate-flavored spreads, as well as portable formats such as Jif To-Go® cups and squeezable pouches. Manufacturing innovations have included a switch from glass to shatterproof, recyclable plastic jars in 1986 and the adoption of molasses as a sweetener in 1971.

The brand has also engaged in partnerships with organizations such as The Peanut Institute (since 1996), the Boys & Girls Clubs of America (since 2003), and served as a sponsor of the U.S. Olympic Team for the 2014 Winter Olympics.

The brand emphasizes simplified ingredients and taste, promoting ''fewer ingredients'' and meeting the FDA standard of 90% peanuts for peanut butter. Its differentiation stems from continuous product innovation—such as the no-utensil squeeze pouch introduced in 2020—and marketing campaigns like the long-running ''Choosy Mothers Choose Jif'' slogan.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Peanut butter manufacturing", "Product formulation and development", "Packaging in plastic jars and squeezable pouches", "Brand licensing and partnerships"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Peanuts", "Molasses", "Chocolate", "Honey (historical)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Meets FDA standard of 90% peanuts for peanut butter", "Molasses used as sweetener instead of honey since 1971", "Shatterproof, recyclable plastic jars reducing shipping emissions since 1986", "Squeezable pouch format for no-utensil snacking introduced in 2020", "Low-sodium, reduced-sugar Simply Jif\u00ae line launched in 1991"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lexington, Kentucky -> db", "Jif brand launched nationally in 1958 -> /about-us", "Product varieties: creamy, crunchy, extra crunchy, natural, reduced fat, Simply Jif, chocolate flavor, Jif To-Go, squeeze pouch -> /about-us and /", "Switch from glass to plastic jars in 1986 -> /about-us", "Use of molasses as sweetener since 1971 -> /about-us", "Partnership with The Peanut Institute since 1996 -> /about-us", "Partnership with Boys & Girls Clubs of America since 2003 -> /about-us", "Sponsor of U.S. Olympic Team 2014 -> /about-us", "Squeeze pouch introduced 2020 -> /about-us", "Simply Jif low sodium, less sugar launched 1991 -> /about-us", "FDA 90% peanut standard met in 1962 -> /about-us", "Choosy Mothers Choose Jif slogan since 1966 -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "The Jif\u00ae brand launches nationally, first with a ''creamy-smooth'' spread and then with a crunchy variety.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-m-smucker-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The J.M. Smucker Co. traces its roots to 1897 in New Bethlehem, Pennsylvania, where Jerome Monroe Smucker pressed cider at his mill and began selling apple butter from a horse-drawn wagon. The business remains under fifth-generation family ownership, with the Smucker family still guiding the company today.

The company manufactures a wide range of food products, including fruit spreads, peanut butters, ice cream toppings, and a portfolio of well-known brands such as Smucker’s, Jif, Folgers, Hostess, Milk-Bone, Meow Mix, and Uncrustables.

The brand portfolio addresses breakfast, snacking, and pet nutrition markets, with items like natural peanut butters, fruit spreads, snack cakes, coffee, and dog and cat treats.

The company emphasizes its long heritage and a commitment to positive impact on employees, communities, and the planet. Its founding principle — “With a name like Smucker’s, it has to be good” — reflects a focus on product quality that has persisted for over 125 years.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fruit spread manufacturing", "Peanut butter manufacturing", "Ice cream topping production", "Natural and organic product formulation", "Multi-brand food production"], "industries": ["Fruit spreads", "Peanut butter", "Coffee", "Snack cakes", "Dog treats", "Cat food"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Two-ingredient natural and organic peanut butters", "Fifth-generation family ownership", "Over 125 years of continuous operation", "Portfolio of iconic brands across multiple food categories"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1897 in New Bethlehem, Pennsylvania -> /about-us", "Founder Jerome Monroe Smucker started with apple butter from horse-drawn wagon -> /about-us", "Fifth-generation family ownership -> /about-us", "Manufactures fruit spreads, peanut butters, ice cream toppings -> /about-us", "Portfolio includes Smucker\u2019s, Jif, Folgers, Hostess, Milk-Bone, Meow Mix, Uncrustables -> /about-us", "Company makes food and snacks for people and pets -> /about-us", "Commitment to positive impact on employees, communities, planet -> /about-us", "Natural and organic peanut butters with two ingredients -> /", "Over 125 years of business success -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "The J.M. Smucker Co. makes food and snacks that people and pets love.", "founded_year": "1897", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-m-smucker-co-2' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J.R.S. Fine Furniture operates from Albuquerque, New Mexico, where a third-generation craftsman continues a family tradition of making rooted in the Rio Grande Valley. The artisan credits grandparents, mother, and father for early lessons in working with wood and other materials, establishing a practice guided by cultural heritage and the surrounding landscape.

The workshop produces one-of-a-kind furniture pieces including dishes, tables, and integrated planters, each handcrafted from materials such as paduk, cherry, hard rock maple, and ash woods, as well as cement, laminate, and brass accents. A growing catalog of available items is complemented by limited custom commissions, and any piece can be reproduced to order.

