UPDATE companies SET description='Janco Electronics Inc. operates from Rollinsford, New Hampshire. In 1966 the company expanded into electronics manufacturing, and in 1985 Lewis E. Janetos incorporated Janco Electronics as a separate entity.

The company provides full-service electronics contract manufacturing and assembly. Core processes include surface‑mount pick‑and‑place, through‑hole technology, fine‑pitch BGA placement and rework, electro‑mechanical system integration, flex‑circuit assembly, conformal coating, and a range of test services such as flying‑probe, in‑circuit, functional, RF/microwave, and 2D X‑ray with 3D capability. Additional offerings cover new‑product introduction (NPI), design‑for‑manufacturability (DFM), cable‑assembly prototyping, supply‑chain management, turnkey assembly, just‑in‑time (JIT) manufacturing, and counterfeit‑component mitigation. Production spans prototype through high‑volume runs.

