UPDATE companies SET description='Kent Metal Fabrication operates from Scottsdale, Arizona. The business was founded by an unnamed owner who had been in the metal fabrication trade since 1998, including over a decade at the family-owned Custom Metal Company. After Custom Metal Cutting was acquired, the owner launched Kent Metal Fabrication to offer custom and production metalwork across the Southwest.

The shop provides a range of fabrication services including welding, plasma cutting, sawing, shearing, torching, drilling, bending on a 100-ton hydraulic press, notching, punching, and custom fabrication. It handles both one-off prototypes and low- to high-volume production runs, and also offers mobile welding and repair work for equipment, trailers, fences, and furniture. The facility is equipped with a hydraulic press brake, a plasma cutting table, and notching equipment.

The company emphasizes quick turnaround and competitive pricing, and it offers a 10–25% discount on first orders to new clients.

