capabilities", "Strategically located service centers, 24/7 availability -> homepage, /about-us", "Built on integrity, long-term partnerships -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Kenwal Steel has grown to operate some of North America''s most successful flat-rolled steel service centers.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/kenwal-steel/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kenwal-steel-tennessee' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kiesub Electronics was founded in 1973 in Las Vegas, Nevada, and has operated continuously from the same industrial center near the Strip. The company began as a wholesale electronics distributor serving the local market and has since expanded its footprint to an 11,000‑square‑foot facility that combines a walk‑in retail store with a manufacturing operation.

Today Kiesub functions as both a broad‑line distributor and a contract manufacturer. The distribution side stocks more than 75,000 electronic parts, components, and accessories, including one of the Southwest’s largest battery inventories. The contract manufacturing division, launched in 1995, produces custom cables, wire harnesses, printed circuit boards, and LED illumination products such as edge‑lit panels and signage for casinos, hotels, and entertainment venues. As a member of the Genie Group purchasing cooperative, Kiesub leverages the buying power of over 90 distributors and 300 locations to source from more than 300 manufacturer accounts.

The customer base spans gaming, entertainment, and hospitality businesses, as well as manufacturers, repair shops, low‑voltage contractors, utilities, school districts, universities, government agencies, and military installations. Hobbyists and walk‑in consumers are also served through the retail counter.

Kiesub emphasizes in‑house design and manufacturing to control quality, and it offers same‑day shipping on in‑stock orders placed before noon Pacific time. The company cites its experienced staff—many with 25‑plus years in the industry—and its Genie Group affiliation as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale electronics distribution", "Custom cable assembly", "Wire harness assembly", "Printed circuit board assembly", "LED illumination manufacturing (edge-lit panels, signs, decor)", "Same-day shipping", "Factory drop-shipping", "Walk-in retail sales", "Battery distribution"], "industries": ["Gaming", "Entertainment", "Hospitality", "Manufacturing", "Repair services", "Low-voltage contracting", "Utilities", "Education", "Government", "Military", "Consumer/hobbyist"], "materials": ["Electronic components", "Batteries", "Cables and wire", "Fiber optic products", "LED panels"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping for in-stock orders placed before 12 PM PST Monday\u2013Friday", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day shipping on in-stock orders placed before 12 PM PST", "Contract manufacturing of custom cables, wire harnesses, PCBs, and LED illumination since 1995", "Genie Group membership providing purchasing power across 90+ distributors and 300+ locations", "11,000 sq ft combined retail store and manufacturing facility", "Over 75,000 electronic parts stocked"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1973 -> /about", "Largest independent wholesale electronics distributor in Nevada -> /about", "Stocks over 75,000 electronic parts -> /about", "Contract manufacturing division began in 1995 -> /about", "Produces custom cables, wire harnesses, PCBs, LED illumination -> /about", "11,000 sq ft store and manufacturing facility -> /about", "Member of Genie Group (90+ distributors, 300+ locations, $1B sales) -> /about", "Same-day shipping on in-stock orders before 12 PM PST -> /about", "Customers include gaming, entertainment, hospitality, government, military -> /about", "Walk-in store open to public -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Kiesub Electronics is a wholesale electronics distributor of electronic equipment, parts and accessories, with a walk-in store that is open to the public.", "founded_year": "1973", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kiesub-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kilo Hollow Energy operates from Ashland, Virginia, serving customers across Virginia, Maryland, Pennsylvania, and Washington, D.C. The company is led by President William Branch and is described as a family-owned business. Founded to provide custom-designed solar and battery systems, the firm focuses on residential and commercial energy independence.

The company designs and installs solar photovoltaic arrays, battery storage systems, and provides electrical service upgrades including 200A and 400A panel changes, EV charger circuits, and generator installations. Its in-house team handles design, permitting, installation, and ongoing maintenance for projects ranging from 4.8 kW residential rooftops to 1 MW commercial arrays. Services also include diagnostics, inverter monitoring, thermal imaging, and system removal or relocation.

Kilo Hollow serves homeowners, businesses, and off-grid clients seeking whole-home backup, grid independence, or reduced utility costs. Commercial customers include property owners looking to offset carbon emissions and enhance market appeal. The firm navigates local codes across its four-state service area and coordinates with utilities for interconnection.

